<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="AgentLair vs. Microsoft AGT, AgentMail, Cloudflare, Lyrie, Experian (re-read Nov 2026)"
      description="How AgentLair compares to Lyrie ATP, ARIA, Experian, AWS AgentCore, Visa TAP, MCP, ERC-8004 — agent identity, credentials, and behavioral trust."
    />
    <meta property="article:modified_time" content="2026-11-09T00:00:00Z" />
    <script type="application/ld+json">{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "AgentLair vs. The Field — Agent Identity and Trust Comparison (corrected Nov 2026)",
  "description": "How AgentLair compares to Lyrie ATP, ARIA, Experian, AWS AgentCore, Visa TAP, MCP, ERC-8004 — agent identity, credentials, and behavioral trust.",
  "datePublished": "2026-05-01",
  "dateModified": "2026-11-09",
  "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "AgentLair", "url": "https://agentlair.dev" },
  "mainEntityOfPage": "https://agentlair.dev/compare",
  "mentions": [
    { "@type": "SoftwareApplication", "name": "Lyrie Agent Trust Protocol", "url": "https://github.com/OTT-Cybersecurity-LLC/lyrie-ai" },
    { "@type": "SoftwareApplication", "name": "ARIA Protocol", "url": "https://aria.bar" },
    { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Experian Agent Trust", "url": "https://www.experianplc.com" }
  ]
}</script>
    <script type="application/ld+json">{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does AgentLair compare to Lyrie ATP?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Lyrie ATP is an open identity standard for agent credentials, with a signed action log per session. AgentLair scores behavior across sessions and organizations. The two fit together: an ATP-credentialed agent with session logs is good input to a cross-org score."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Experian Agent Trust a replacement for AgentLair?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Not outside commerce. Experian binds a verified human to an agent and, per its announcement, adjusts the agent's trust score over time from behavioral signals across merchants in its network. It does not read tool-call logs or cover non-commerce work across organizations, which is where AgentLair operates."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does AgentLair do that Lyrie, ARIA, and Experian don't?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A behavioral score built across organizations and sessions. Lyrie logs one session, ARIA signs per-operation receipts, Experian scores inside commerce."
      }
    }
  ]
}</script>
